5.4.1   Verification of the Significance of Momentum
     To assess the role of momentum in tennis, we apply the Constant Win Probability (CWP)
     微

                                         M


model by setting 𝜂(𝑆 𝑚 ) = 1 in the Real-Time Win Probability (RTWP) model, thereby disregarding
all in-match factors including momentum. We then consider the outcome of the CWP model as
our observed value. If the coach’s assertion is incorrect, the residuals (the differences between
                               ：




the predicted and observed outcomes) would deviate from a normal distribution, indicating a
discrepancy between the models and the observed results. We employ both qualitative (probability
                       号




distribution plots of the residuals) and quantitative (K-S test) methods to evaluate the validity of the
coach’s hypothesis. If the coach’s claim is disproven, it confirms the existence and significance
of momentum in tennis matches, thereby validating the effectiveness of our RTWP and RTMQ
               信




models.
