7.2    Model Setup




                                                                                      型
    Mixed Strategies. A mixed strategy for player 𝑖 is defined as a probability distribution over the
set of pure strategies. Let 𝑛𝑖 denote the number of pure strategies available to player 𝑖. A mixed
strategy for player 𝑖 (the player is a server or a receiver) can then be represented as a vector




                                                                             模
                                           p𝑖 = ( 𝑝𝑖1 , 𝑝𝑖2 , ..., 𝑝𝑖𝑛𝑖 )                                    (15)




                                                                            学
where 𝑝𝑖 𝑗 is the probability that player 𝑖 will play pure strategy 𝑗. These probabilities are non-
negative and sum to 1
                                                    𝑛𝑖




                                                                 数
                                                   ∑︁
                                       𝑝𝑖 𝑗 ≥ 0,       𝑝𝑖 𝑗 = 1                                (16)
                                                           𝑗=1



                                          ：
    Expected Payoffs. The expected payoff for player 𝑖 given a profile of mixed strategies p is




                                                                               els
calculated as the sum of the payoffs for each possible outcome, weighted by the probability of that
                                         号
outcome. If 𝑢𝑖 (𝑠1 , ..., 𝑠𝑛 ) denotes the payoff to player 𝑖 for strategy profile (𝑠1 , ..., 𝑠𝑛 ), the expected
payoff is given by:




                                                                             od
                                              ∑︁ ∑︁                        𝑛
                                                                           Ö
                                众

                                 𝐸 [𝑢𝑖 (p)] =    ...    𝑢𝑖 (𝑠1 , ..., 𝑠𝑛 )   𝑝 𝑗𝑠𝑗                          (17)
                                              𝑠1      𝑠𝑛
                                                                            m
                                                                            𝑗=1
                       公


   Best Responses. A best response for player 𝑖 is a strategy that maximizes player 𝑖’s expected
                                                        H
payoff, given the strategies of the other players. Formally, a best response p𝑖∗ satisfies
                                                     AT
       信




                                        p𝑖∗ ∈ arg max 𝐸 [𝑢𝑖 (p𝑖 , p−𝑖 )]                                     (18)
                                                     p𝑖
      微




    Nash Equilibrium. A mixed-strategy Nash equilibrium is a strategy profile where every
                                            M



player’s strategy is a best response to the strategies of the other players. Formally, a strategy profile
p∗ = (p∗1 , ..., p∗𝑛 ) is a Nash equilibrium if and only if for all 𝑖
                                  ：




                                        p𝑖∗ ∈ arg max 𝐸 [𝑢𝑖 (p𝑖 , p∗−𝑖 )]                                    (19)
                                                     p𝑖
                         号




In other words, no player can improve their expected payoff by unilaterally deviating from their
equilibrium strategy. Bringing our strategies into the model, the probability combination of
